CatPaw (国际版) Linux port — unofficial

This package repackages the official CatPaw overseas macOS build
(catpaw.20260929170804.dmg) into a Linux Electron application. It is not
published or supported by CatPaw/Meituan.

Differences from the upstream build:
- Electron, Node.js, CPython, and native modules are replaced with official
  Linux builds; node-pty, bufferutil, and utf-8-validate are compiled locally
  against Electron headers. No network access happens during build.
- The packaged @catpaw/agent-sdk CLI binary is replaced with the Linux build
  published by the same upstream CLI project. If the international gateway
  rejects it, report the issue instead of downgrading the package silently.
- The macOS-only xlsx-sidecar binary is not installed. Spreadsheet-heavy
  features that depend on it (Excel formula evaluation, sheet-to-image
  rendering) are unavailable on Linux; opening, editing, and saving xlsx still
  use the bundled JS implementation.
- The app runs with --no-sandbox because the Arch package cannot carry the
  upstream setuid helper in a portable way. Do not use it for untrusted content
  if you require Chromium's sandbox.

Identity isolation from the Chinese edition (catpaw-cn):
- applicationName / WM class: catpaw-overseas
- data directory: ~/.catpaw-overseas
- appId: com.catx.catpaw.overseas
- desktop file and icon: catpaw-overseas

This package does not declare the catpaw-app URL scheme in its desktop entry.
The application may still attempt to register itself at runtime; without a
MimeType declaration that usually fails silently. Both editions can be
installed side by side without a declared handler conflict.

Upstream does not publish an EULA for this build. The repackaging scripts in
this package are licensed under LICENSE.port-scripts; the bundled application
remains subject to its upstream terms.
